% ============================================================================
% galaxy-types.query.adj — a worked recall over the astronomy galaxy-types library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does a spiral galaxy
% look like?": it states no astronomy fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `galaxy_shape` rows and returns the shape + the table's source/locator/
% trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the shape
% `round_to_oval`, recall its galaxy type — elliptical). A word that is not one
% of the main galaxy types abstains honestly — the engine never invents a shape.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli galaxy-types.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "galaxy-types.adj"

? galaxy_shape(spiral, $Shape)         % expect spiral_arms
? galaxy_shape(elliptical, $Shape)     % expect round_to_oval
? galaxy_shape(irregular, $Shape)      % expect unusual_shapes
? galaxy_shape($Type, round_to_oval)   % reverse bind — expect elliptical
? galaxy_shape(planet, $Shape)         % expect abstain — a planet is not a galaxy type
